### How Character Illustrations Are Used

```
HOME SCREEN:
  → Shows character matching current mood log (e.g., char_happy, char_tired)
  → If no mood logged yet: char_hello (waving good morning)
  → During period: char_cozy or char_cramps based on logged symptoms
  → Ovulation phase: char_happy or char_excited

DAILY LOG SCREEN:
  → Mood selector shows character thumbnails instead of just emojis
  → Selecting "tired" shows char_tired as preview
  → Selecting "cramps" symptom highlights char_cramps

FROM HIM SCREEN:
  → char_in_love as hero illustration
  → When opening envelope: char_shy or char_excited
  → After reading message: char_grateful

CYCLE SCREEN:
  → Phase-specific character:
    Menstrual: char_cozy or char_cramps
    Follicular: char_waking_up
    Ovulation: char_excited or char_happy
    Luteal: char_deep_breath or char_content

MOOD GARDEN:
  → Garden has mini character version tending flowers
  → Character shows char_content when garden is thriving
  → char_sad when no logs for 3+ days

EMPTY STATES:
  → char_hello for first-time screens
  → char_journaling for empty journal
  → char_planning for empty cycle data

ONBOARDING:
  → Sequence: char_hello → char_happy → char_in_love (final reveal screen)

AI COMPANION:
  → Companion avatar cycles through relevant characters during chat
  → Responding to cramps: char_cozy + warmth suggestions
  → Responding to sadness: char_in_love + his message preview

SELF-CARE SECTION:
  → char_bath_time for bath suggestions
  → char_skin_care for skincare
  → char_music_time for music recommendations
  → char_meditating for meditation mode

INSIGHTS / REPORTS:
  → char_productive when streaks are good
  → char_content when cycle is regular
```

