## 8. APP ARCHITECTURE

### Layer Pattern (per feature)

```
Presentation → Riverpod AsyncNotifier + Widgets + Pages
    ↓ calls
Domain → Freezed models + Repository interfaces (abstract)
    ↓ implemented by
Data → Repository impl + Remote DS (Firebase) + Local DS (Drift/Hive)
    ↓ uses
Core → Firebase services, AI service, encryption, notifications
```

### Riverpod Patterns

```dart
// All features use AsyncNotifier
@riverpod
class DailyLogNotifier extends _$DailyLogNotifier {
  @override
  Future<DailyLogEntry?> build(DateTime date) async {
    return ref.watch(logRepositoryProvider).getLogForDate(date);
  }
  Future<void> save(DailyLogEntry entry) async {
    state = const AsyncLoading();
    state = await AsyncValue.guard(() => ref.read(logRepositoryProvider).save(entry));
  }
}

// In widgets: ALWAYS handle all 3 states
ref.watch(dailyLogProvider(date)).when(
  data: (log) => LogContent(log: log),
  loading: () => LunaLoading(),
  error: (e, _) => LunaEmptyState(illustration: AppIllustrations.sad, ...),
)

// Side effects: use ref.listen()
ref.listen(saveProvider, (_, next) {
  if (next is AsyncData) {
    HapticFeedback.lightImpact();
    showSaveAnimation();
  }
});
```

