## 17. DO'S AND DON'TS

### DO ✅
- Use `IllustratedCard` for every major card — character presence everywhere
- Use `AppIllustrations.forMood()`, `.forCyclePhase()`, `.forSymptom()` for character selection
- Support placeholder mode in `IllustratedCard` until real assets arrive
- `const` constructors everywhere possible
- Handle all `AsyncValue` states: data + loading + error — always
- Use `ref.listen()` for side effects, `ref.watch()` in build
- `Freezed` for all data models
- `Result<T>` for repository returns
- `GoRouter` named routes only (define all names in `app_routes.dart`)
- `HapticFeedback.lightImpact()` on all primary interactions
- `HapticFeedback.mediumImpact()` on saves and completions
- Drift local DB first, Firestore sync second (offline-first)
- `flutter_secure_storage` for PIN and encryption key
- Cormorant Garamond for emotional display text — always
- Caveat font for anything "from him" — always
- Rose-tinted shadows (never gray shadows)
- Character thumbnails (32px) on mood chips and symptom chips
- The `from_him` section must always feel premium — never rush it
- Write warm, personal copy for ALL empty states and notifications
- Test the envelope open animation frame-by-frame before shipping Phase 4

### DON'T ❌
- Don't use `GetX`, `Provider`, `BLoC` — Riverpod only
- Don't call `ref.read()` inside `build()` — use `ref.watch()`
- Don't use `Navigator.push()` — GoRouter only
- Don't put business logic in widgets
- Don't store encryption keys anywhere (Firestore, Hive, SharedPrefs)
- Don't use generic fonts (Inter, Roboto, System)
- Don't use gray shadows anywhere — all shadows are rose-tinted
- Don't show blank/empty screens — LunaEmptyState on every zero state
- Don't use `FutureBuilder`/`StreamBuilder` — AsyncValue only
- Don't show raw numbers without warm card context
- Don't skip haptics
- Don't use bubblegum pink (#FF69B4) — use the warm dusty rose palette
- Don't build the From Him section quickly — it's the emotional core
- Don't add placeholder text that doesn't make sense warmly
  BAD: "No data" / "Loading..." / "Error occurred"
  GOOD: "He hasn't left anything here yet 🌸" / Shimmer / Soft error illustration

